## 📋 Requirements & Setup

Make sure you have Python 3.8+ installed on your system. 

1. Install the official `cryptography` dependency library:
   ```bash
   pip install cryptography
   ```

2. Clone this repository or copy the implementation code file (`main.py`) locally.

---

## 💻 Usage Instructions

Run the script directly via your command line interface:

```bash
python main.py
```

### 1. Session Initialization (Login)
When starting up, you will be requested to establish your cryptographic context window:
```text
=======================================================
+++++++++++++++ WELCOME TO LOGIN PAGE +++++++++++++++++
=======================================================
++Enter user name :- secure_user
++Enter password :- MySuperSecurePassword123!
++Enter your MEMORY KEY :- secret_phrase_alpha
```

### 2. Modes of Operation
After initializing your cryptographic identity parameters, select your target workspace mode:

* Type **`-a`** to enter data addition mode.
* Type **`-o`** to enter vault decryption and entry opening mode.

#### Adding Records (`-a`):
```text
[+++++++++++++== PLEASE ADD NEW INFO ==+++++++++++++]

++Enter Website name :- github.com
++Enter Website user name :- git_dev
++Enter Website Password :- gHp_SecureTokenExample992!

✔ [SYSTEM]: Encrypted & saved data permanently to disk for github.com!
Please enter Y to add new info or enter N [Y/N] :- n
```

#### Opening Records (`-o`):
```text
================ VAULT Opening =================
++Enter Website name to decrypt :- github.com

 ===]-->> Decryption Successful <<--[=== 
Website: github.com
Username: git_dev
Password: gHp_SecureTokenExample992!      
```

